{"title":"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the length and width of a rectangle are each increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, then the perimeter of the rectangle is increased by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13be02722b7cb8b320b760c1c097939a8ee7f0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 1\\% \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 10\\% \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 20\\% \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 21\\% \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"442\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the original width, length, and perimeter of the rectangle, respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/936fc074cd88aca5e9a6c14a8b3727ad7f2ffebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2(w+l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>The width and length are increased to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1ac26d25817bb908a7092bd274f1618f64a491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1w$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba894627be75071c1d8b7e0bc5d370b1b6054dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1l$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Therefore, the new perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd23a3d24b81554189649e854275131c4b00dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1.1w+1.1l)=2\\cdot1.1(w+l) = 1.1 \\cdot 2(w+l) = 1.1p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"420\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddce32c59beb38784636b2cc1549e012152890f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"31\" /> more than the original perimeter.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each side is scaled by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8947103eef4bf1bdd05314762d33e9913e6840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, the new rectangle is similar to the original, and therefore its perimeter is also scaled by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8947103eef4bf1bdd05314762d33e9913e6840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, that is, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddce32c59beb38784636b2cc1549e012152890f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"31\" /> increase.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the original rectangle is a square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so its perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebce7411e09d7d7308fab601f4e547431f6f67c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 10 = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />.  After scaling, its sides will have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eeee09163719b6b1288eb1ed3c9f22d2f3e8a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.1 \\cdot 10 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />, so its perimeter will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d94ab61205f47dd4d47e47a5eba1768261db8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 4 = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the new perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533306a7e7a01259a852f000e6009ece0429bf87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{44}{40} = 1.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" /> times the original perimeter, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddce32c59beb38784636b2cc1549e012152890f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"31\" /> increase.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jAy9O53u-nQ\">https://youtu.be/jAy9O53u-nQ</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME\" title=\"1985 AJHSME\">1985 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017102626\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.087 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 167/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3545/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.238      1 -total\n 58.56%    8.338      1 Template